  "notes": "Measured on the E175 N106SY (left, Dec 2025), checked on N162SY (Jul 2026); CRJs (N925EV, N642RW's E170) show the same. Unlike the mainline's gray engines with a blue ring, the regional jets' engines are white with a bare lip. The gold line's path and the globe are kept from standard-2010. The small 'Operated by SkyWest' under the cockpit is not drawn. Positions are measured on E175s, whose window line is higher (y about 0.3) than the narrow-body average in COORDINATES.md, so titles placed above or below the windows sit higher than they would on a 737. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the gold line (kept from the mainline's, which was wrong for both) redrawn on N106SY: it follows the same path as the 2019 regional scheme's navy line, just under both doors' sills and low under the tail (heights taken from N624UX's measured line, which N106SY matches against the doors).",
  "history": "The 2010 scheme on United Express jets; being replaced by the 2019 scheme (express) as they are repainted."
